      "writtenOn": "2022-08-04T04:54:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I struggle to understand this. IIUC, framework-connectivity-t is allowed to reference the full framework-connectivity ; do you mean here that this is what we should do, but it\u0027s not done yet ? I expect that\u0027s not what you mean because in this context I don\u0027t see what being \"also part of the stubs\" has to do with this. Do you mean we are splitting classes between these that are part of the public API and these that are not, and for these that are part of the public API we only generate stubs and therefore hidden symbols are not there ? But if that\u0027s right, shouldn\u0027t the classes that are part of the public API *also* be in the full impl framework-connectivity.jar and that should be the only artifact referenced by framework-connectivity-t ?\n\nI\u0027m sorry I\u0027m lacking context but these things are so horribly confusing that even with extensive explanations like this it will be extremely hard for someone to understand one year down the road.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 24,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 25,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "77d4c4efa87321d85f482b7bd9e5779f20b28690",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d989ef1c_856d8551",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 25,
      "author": {
        "id": 1288034
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-09T08:22:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e framework-connectivity-t is allowed to reference the full framework-connectivity ; do you mean here that this is what we should do, but it\u0027s not done yet ?\n \nYes, this was not actually fully possible in framework-connectivity-t-pre-jarjar before, because it had \"sdk_module-lib_current_framework-connectivity\" (the SDK stubs) in its libs *before* framework-connectivity-pre-jarjar; so it would build against the stubs of ConnectivityManager instead of the full ConnectivityManager. Classes that are fully hidden and not part of the stubs (like KeepaliveUtils or DnsUtils) would not be a problem though, and be usable from framework-connectivity-pre-jarjar. That\u0027s why \"also part of the stubs\" matters, because there\u0027s a conflict for classes that are in both the stubs and framework-connectivity-pre-jarjar, and the stubs are used in priority.\n\n \u003e Do you mean we are splitting classes between these that are part of the public API and these that are not, and for these that are part of the public API we only generate stubs and therefore hidden symbols are not there ?\n\nRight, the stubs only contain classes that are part of the API\n\n \u003e shouldn\u0027t the classes that are part of the public API *also* be in the full impl framework-connectivity.jar and that should be the only artifact referenced by framework-connectivity-t ?\n\nframework-connectivity-t.impl does reference the full (pre-jarjar) impl library framework-connectivity-pre-jarjar via \"impl_only_libs\"; but it can\u0027t use it to build the stubs, since there would be a circular dependency (framework-connectivity-pre-jarjar uses framework-connectivity-t.stubs.module_lib).",
      "parentUuid": "cbdf8f29_ac9dc581",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 24,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 25,
        "endChar": 31
      },
